                "{\"score\": 6, \"reasoning\": \"All four required panels are present and readable, with two useful additional panels. The histograms shift from higher to lower Q with increasing temperature, and heat capacity varies nontrivially, although it is coarsely sampled. The final chain appears connected but spread out, with long bonds and numerous projected crossings; the lack of 3D axes makes compactness difficult to assess. The reported transition is explicitly defined by mean Q=0.5, but does not coincide with the heat-capacity maximum. The free-energy curve has repeated sharp spikes and a broad central minimum rather than clearly resolved folding basins and a meaningful barrier. Similar spikes occur in the reference, but neither establishes convincing basin/barrier structure.\"}"
